Restore bounded manager-5/V3 coredump handling in both retained ABI backends.

Attribute fault and completion interrupts to the exact TCB range, distinguish
waiting, signalled, and completed states, bound the completion wait to five
seconds, serialize command-pool recovery before jobs are reaped, and prevent
one coredump job from indefinitely suppressing pool teardown.  The same state
model also covers close, abort, timeout, and later scheduling decisions.

Preserve the public CIX V3 coredump ABI and userspace control flow, but replace
the vendor driver's cross-job attribution and unbounded wait with explicit
lifetime and recovery boundaries. Deliberate hardware fault testing remains a
separate, explicitly disruptive qualification step.

